+# Generation prompts
+
+Generated fresh from text using the built-in image generation tool. No reference images.
+
+## 269-travel-poster.png
+
+Create one square 1024x1024 image fresh from text, without any reference image. Authentic 1930s WPA national park travel poster made by silkscreen printing. Let the historical graphic medium fully govern anatomy, composition, and palette: bold angular simplified mountains, towering flat pine silhouettes, broad flat fields of deep forest green, muted teal, ochre, terracotta, and cream; limited spot-color printing, subtle ink-on-paper grain, strong diagonal trail and monumental cropped landforms. Wide landscape scene in a square poster format, a full-body woman hiking along the foreground trail in three-quarter profile, pausing to enjoy coffee from her thermos cup; thermos in the other hand and a croissant visible in the open top of her hiking pack. She is early 30s, shoulder-length curly auburn hair, freckles, round tortoiseshell glasses, mustard-yellow knit sweater. Her features and knit texture are reduced to crisp graphic shapes appropriate to an authentic WPA print. The park and mountains dominate; her figure is integrated into the bold shape composition, not a photographic portrait. No text of any kind, no title, no lettering, no numbers, no captions, no signatures, no watermarks. Fill the square with the illustrated poster itself, not a photographed or framed poster.
+
+## 270-coloring-book.png
+
+Generate one fresh text-only image, square 1024x1024, no image references. A children's coloring book page, viewed directly from above, filling almost the whole square. The page's art is charming, extremely simple cartoon line art: heavy clean rounded black outlines, oversized friendly head and hands, simplified anatomy and shapes, big easy-to-color empty white spaces, no hatching, no shading in the printed line work. It shows a woman in her early 30s with shoulder-length curly auburn hair, freckles, round tortoiseshell glasses, a mustard-yellow knit sweater, sitting at a simple round cafe table, smiling with eyes softly closed as she enjoys a large coffee cup held in both hands; a large croissant on a plate nearby. Medium seated front-facing cartoon composition. About HALF of the picture has been colored by a child with visible rough wax-crayon scribbles and some strokes outside the outlines: auburn curls, brown-and-amber glasses, mustard-yellow sweater, a little golden pastry and a few bright table accents; the other half remains genuinely untouched white paper within thick outlines. Leave part of the hair, sweater, and table uncolored so unfinished coloring is obvious. Several real wax crayons lie diagonally on the page along the edges, clearly physical crayons with subtle contact shadows, wrappers entirely blank. The page artwork must look like a real children's coloring book, never a realistic portrait with a filter. Sparse composition, large open white areas, joyful simplicity. No printed or handwritten words, no letters, no numbers, no captions, no signatures, no watermarks anywhere.
+
+## 271-naturalist-plate.png
+
+Create one entirely fresh image from text only, no reference images, square 1024x1024. An authentic 19th-century naturalist illustration plate on warm ivory rag paper: intricate copperplate engraving with very fine burin lines, crosshatching and stippling, restrained translucent hand-applied watercolor washes. Arrange the elements like a botanical specimen study with generous unprinted margins and detached detail vignettes, no continuous environment. The main specimen is a waist-up woman in her early 30s in elegant strict side profile facing left, lifting a delicate coffee cup toward her lips and enjoying its aroma; curly shoulder-length auburn hair, freckles rendered as stipple, round tortoiseshell glasses, mustard-yellow knit sweater with its knit engraved in fine linework. Surround this profile study with carefully observed arching coffee plant branches, glossy leaves, red coffee cherries, white star-shaped flowers, isolated brown coffee beans, a bisected coffee berry and magnified blossom details. A small croissant is presented nearby as its own hand-colored engraved specimen. Some fine technical leader lines extend from selected visible features of the woman (hair curl, eyeglass rim, sweater knit) and from botanical parts into empty margin space, giving the visual arrangement of labeled specimen parts, BUT absolutely no actual labels or text, no letterlike symbols, no numbers, no handwriting. Muted botanical greens, soft sepia, auburn, ochre, a few vermilion berries. The human figure must be drawn as a period engraved scientific illustration, not photorealistic, not a photograph with an antique effect. Square plate fills the image. No captions, no headings, no border lettering, no signatures, no watermarks.
+
+## 272-pysanka.png
+
+Generate a fresh square 1024x1024 image from text alone with NO reference images. Ukrainian pysanka folk craft: a single beautifully decorated egg resting at a slight diagonal on softly folded traditional red-and-black embroidered ivory linen. Close object composition, the egg dominates the square, its entire oval silhouette clearly visible. Authentic intricate wax-resist decoration wraps around the curved shell: precise fine yellow and cream reserved lines on rich black and vermilion red fields, nested geometric bands, tiny triangular teeth, eight-pointed rosettes, stylized floral sprigs, dots and latticework. Slight handmade irregularity in the wax-drawn lines, subtle eggshell texture, rich dye colors; no gems or metal, no Faberge aesthetic. A prominent oval medallion integrated into the egg's wax-resist ornament contains a FLAT FOLK-ART portrait of a woman in her early 30s enjoying coffee: shoulder-length curly auburn hair expressed as ornamental reddish curls, freckles as tiny dots, round tortoiseshell glasses as patterned rings, mustard-yellow knit sweater as yellow fields with rhythmic little stitch chevrons. She cradles a tiny decorated coffee cup near her delighted face; a stylized croissant motif sits next to her within the medallion. The woman exists only as graphic wax-resist artwork ON the egg, not a live person, not a photographic portrait pasted onto it. All portrait anatomy is governed by handmade folk design: simplified face, ornamental hair, flattened forms, expressive large eyes, compressed proportions fitted to the oval. Soft warm side light shows the rounded egg and the red cross-stitch threads on the cloth; restrained background, intimate craft still life. Strong red, black, yellow palette with tiny ivory accents. No words, no letters, no numbers, no captions, no signatures, no watermark.
+

